<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-103>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-103" ;
  triage:title "v1.3-consumer compatibility fixture materially thinner than AC9's own wording" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-http-runtime/tests/http_v1_3_compat.rs only asserts major-version equality and that one pre-AZ route still resolves. It does not test 'every pre-AZ route,' does not test that a 1.3.0 client ignores additive task response fields, and does not test the sprint's own explicitly required behavior: 'New task requests sent to a 1.3.0 daemon fail with the existing typed unsupported-route/version response before mutation.' Confirmed at head 6937c547f. Fix: expand http_v1_3_compat.rs to cover all three gaps per AC9's own wording. Source: QA-1 on PR #1382 (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1382#issuecomment-5612459494). STILL OPEN at QA-2 (head b8900296c): the fix pass retargeted the fixture to the 1.4.0 baseline but its new test filters the *current* route list to remove /v1/atm/tasks and asserts the filtered list lacks it -- a tautology by construction, not a behavioral proof of an older-version router rejecting the route. No test proves a 1.4.0 consumer ignores additive task response fields. AC9 remains unsatisfied. Source: QA-2 on PR #1382." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
